<figure class="fixture-study" aria-labelledby="fixture-study-title">
  <figcaption id="fixture-study-title">
    <span>TEST MATRIX / LITTLE-ENDIAN FORMAT</span>
    <strong>A passing round trip can still produce wrong bytes</strong>
  </figcaption>
  <p>Fixture for integer <code>0x1234</code>: offset +0 is <code>34</code>, offset +1 is <code>12</code>.</p>
  <dl class="cases">
    <div><dt>Correct LE encoder + decoder</dt><dd><code>0x1234 → 34 12 → 0x1234</code></dd><dd>Round trip: <strong>pass</strong>. Golden bytes: <strong>pass</strong>.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Wrong BE encoder + decoder</dt><dd><code>0x1234 → 12 34 → 0x1234</code></dd><dd>Round trip: <strong>pass</strong>. Golden bytes: <strong>fail</strong>.</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p>Test decoding the independent fixture too: the wrong decoder reads <code>34 12</code> as <code>0x3412</code>.</p>
</figure>

